## Factoradic Structure

Every integer n has a unique representation n = Σ a_k · k! with 0 ≤ a_k ≤ k. The digit sum is S_!(n) = Σ a_k.

Since 6! = 720, numbers 0 to 719 use digits a_1 (0–1), a_2 (0–2), a_3 (0–3), a_4 (0–4), a_5 (0–5), with max value 5·120+4·24+3·6+2·2+1·1 = 719.

